    "id": "arp-apq-m3-007",
    "type": "APQ",
    "module": "Module3",
    "source": "M3 Assessment Practice Question 7",
    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-apq-m3-007-q-1.png\" alt=\"Question 7\n\nCompanies A and B\n\nYou are the adviser to two companies. Neither company had a deferred tax balance at 31 March 20X1\nand both prepare financial statements in accordance with IFRS Accounting Standards.\n\nCompany A has an asset that cost £1,000,000 on 1 April 20X1. It is being depreciated over its 10-year\nuseful life, using the straight-line method.\n\nCompany B also has an asset that cost £1,000,000 on 1 April 20X1. It is being depreciated over its 3-\nyear useful life, using the straight-line method.\n\nBoth assets qualify for capital allowances. The writing-down allowance rate is 18%. The deferred tax\nrate is 25%.\n\nRequired:\n\nCalculate the deferred tax asset or liability at 31 March 20X2, 20X3 and 20X4, and prepare the\nnecessary journal entry for the year ended 31 March 20X4 for each company.\n\n                                                                                            (9 marks)\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                 7\">",
    "a": "<img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-apq-m3-007-a-1.png\" alt=\"Question 7: Solution\n\nCompanies A and B\n\nCarrying amount\n\n                                                    Company A  Company B\n                                                                          £’000        £’000\nCost (1 April 20X1)                                                         1,000        1,000\nDepreciation charge (1/10 years x £1,000,000)/(1/3 years x £1,000,000)         (100)         (333)\nCarrying amount (31 March 20X2)                                         900         667\nDepreciation charge                                                             (100)         (333)\nCarrying amount (31 March 20X3)                                         800         334\nDepreciation charge                                                             (100)         (334)\nCarrying amount (31 March 20X4)                                         700                   -\n\n                                                                                            (2 marks)\n\nTax written-down value\n\n                                                              Companies A and B\n                                                                                       £’000\nCost (1 April 20X1)                                                                       1,000\nCapital allowances (18% x £1,000k)                                                            (180)\nTax written-down value (31 March 20X2)                                                 820\nCapital allowances (18% x £820k)                                                              (148)\nTax written-down value (31 March 20X3)                                                 672\nCapital allowances (18% x £672k)                                                              (121)\nTax written-down value (31 March 20X4)                                                 551\n\n                                                                                             (1 mark)\n\nDeferred tax\n\nCompany A\n\n                                                                       Taxable/\n                                                                         (deductible)\n                                           Carrying                temporary  Deferred tax\n                                    amount     Tax base    difference liability/ asset\n                                              £’000         £’000         £’000        £’000\n31 March 20X2                               900         820          80       20 Cr\n31 March 20X3                               800         672         128       32 Cr\n31 March 20X4                               700         551         149       37 Cr\nIncrease in deferred tax liability in 20X4                                               5\n\n                                                                                            (2 marks)\n\nCompany B\n\n31 March 20X2                                     667       820       (153)      38 Dr\n31 March 20X3                                     334       672       (338)      85 Dr\n31 March 20X4                                                                -       551       (551)     138 Dr\nIncrease in deferred tax asset in 20X4                                                 53\n\n                                                                                            (2 marks)\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                11\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-apq-m3-007-a-2.png\" alt=\"Journal entries\n\nCompany A\n\n                                                                           £’000     £’000\nDr  SPL – income tax expense                                             5\n    Cr Deferred tax liability                                                          5\nBeing increase in deferred tax liability for year to 31 March 20X4\n\n                                                                                             (1 mark)\n\nCompany B\n\nDr  Deferred tax asset                                           53\n    Cr SPL – income tax expense                                                    53\nBeing increase in deferred tax asset for year to 31 March 20X4\n\n                                                                                             (1 mark)\n\n                                                                            Total marks (9 marks)\n\n\n\n\n\n12\">",
